#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Improving Expectation Values: Propagated Noise Absorption (PNA)"
msgstr "Mejora de Valores Esperados: Absorción de Ruido Propagado (PNA)"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-"
"addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-"
"addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will learn how to leverage the latest tools in the "
"Qiskit ecosystem to implement a fully customizable, error mitigated "
"workflow. We will introduce the PNA technique and use it to mitigate gate "
"errors. We will also use TREX to mitigate readout errors and post-selection "
"to mitigate errors not captured in the learned noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"En este tutorial, aprenderemos a aprovechar las últimas herramientas del "
"ecosistema Qiskit para implementar un flujo de trabajo completamente "
"personalizable con mitigación de errores. Presentaremos la técnica PNA y la "
"usaremos para mitigar errores de compuerta. También usaremos TREX para "
"mitigar errores de lectura y post-selección para mitigar errores no "
"capturados en el modelo de ruido aprendido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Outline**\n"
"- Give a brief overview of ``PNA``\n"
"- Create a Trotterized quantum circuit and observable. Transpile it to the backend and include post-selection measurements.\n"
"- Use ``samplomatic`` to twirl layers of 2Q gates and measurements. Find unique 2Q layers to reduce noise learning cost.\n"
"- Use ``NoiseLearnerV3`` to learn the error model affecting the 2Q gates and measurements.\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-pna`` to generate a noise-mitigating observable\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` primitive to generate the raw QPU samples reflecting every shot for every twirling randomization and measured basis\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-utils`` to post-process the data into a mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Esquema**\n"
"- Dar una breve descripción general de ``PNA``\n"
"- Crear un circuito cuántico Trotterizado y un observable. Transpilarlo al backend e incluir mediciones de post-selección.\n"
"- Usar ``samplomatic`` para aplicar twirling a capas de compuertas de 2 qubits y mediciones. Encontrar capas de 2 qubits únicas para reducir el costo de aprendizaje del ruido.\n"
"- Usar ``NoiseLearnerV3`` para aprender el modelo de error que afecta a las compuertas de 2 qubits y las mediciones.\n"
"- Usar ``qiskit-addon-pna`` para generar un observable que mitigue el ruido\n"
"- Usar el primitivo ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` para generar las muestras brutas de la QPU que reflejen cada disparo para cada aleatorización de twirling y base medida\n"
"- Usar ``qiskit-addon-utils`` para post-procesar los datos en un valor esperado mitigado.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-"
"absorption-pna}"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué es la absorción de ruido propagado (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-"
"absorption-pna}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"***A technique for mitigating gate errors by propagating the observable through the inverse noise channel affecting 2-qubit gates, resulting in a noise-mitigating observable.***\n"
"The 2Q gates in the experiment we want to run will be affected by substantial noise.\n"
"![Noisy experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"If we learn the noise model, we can apply its inverse and cancel the noise.\n"
"![Noise-mitigated experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"Instead of implementing the inverse noise channel by sampling it on the QPU as in PEC, we can implement it classically in the measured observable using Pauli propagation. This results in a more complex observable which, when measured, has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise.\n"
"![PNA overview](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"***Una técnica para mitigar errores de compuerta propagando el observable a través del canal de ruido inverso que afecta a las compuertas de 2 qubits, resultando en un observable que mitiga el ruido.***\n"
"Las compuertas de 2 qubits en el experimento que queremos ejecutar se verán afectadas por un ruido considerable.\n"
"![Noisy experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"Si aprendemos el modelo de ruido, podemos aplicar su inverso y cancelar el ruido.\n"
"![Noise-mitigated experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"En lugar de implementar el canal de ruido inverso muestreándolo en la QPU como en PEC, podemos implementarlo clásicamente en el observable medido usando propagación de Pauli. Esto resulta en un observable más complejo que, cuando se mide, tiene el efecto de mitigar el ruido de compuerta aprendido.\n"
"![PNA overview](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate the mirrored Trotter circuit and observable {#generate-the-"
"mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr ""
"Generar el circuito de Trotter en espejo y el observable {#generate-the-"
"mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this experiment, we will study the time dynamics of a 30-site kicked "
"Ising model on a 1D spin chain. The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para este experimento, estudiaremos la dinámica temporal de un modelo de "
"Ising pateado de 30 sitios en una cadena de espines 1D. El Hamiltoniano "
"considerado es:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and the"
" global transverse field, $h$, is set to $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. The further $h$ "
"is from a Clifford angle (i.e. $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}$), the more difficult it becomes to propagate the anti-noise "
"generators through the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $J>0$ describe el acoplamiento de espines vecinos más cercanos, $i<j$,"
" y el campo transversal global, $h$, se establece en $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. "
"Cuanto más lejos esté $h$ de un ángulo de Clifford (es decir, "
"$\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), más difícil será propagar "
"los generadores anti-ruido a través del circuito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the choice of observable, we will consider the average single-site "
"magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, where "
"$N$ is the number of sites.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para la elección del observable, consideraremos la magnetización promedio de"
" un solo sitio, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, donde "
"$N$ es el número de sitios.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-"
"mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-"
"mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will choose a chain of qubits on ``ibm_kingston`` that report low "
"error rates and transpile the circuit to the backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, elegiremos una cadena de qubits en ``ibm_kingston`` que "
"reporten tasas de error bajas y transpilaremos el circuito al backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-"
